# Lumenhold Academy — 简体中文 (zh-CN) translation of content/events/pools/village_more.grim
# Maintained by `node tools/grim.js i18n zh-CN`. Translate the text after "="; keep {tokens}.
# "# en:" shows the English source. [hash] marks the English version a line was translated from;
# lines marked STALE need updating — after fixing the text, delete the [hash] and re-run the tool.


@event gilded_newt_ballad
# en: The Newt's Ballad
title [13f4ec] = 蝾螈之歌
# en: {An old regular is standing on a bench singing the ballad of the Newt, about the fire that never goes out. It has forty verses. He knows most of them.|The ballad again. Tonight it has forty-one verses; the new one is about a student who fell into the cellar.|The ballad has a verse about the castle now, and the regulars look at you when they reach it.} {The landlady pretends to hate it.|The whole room bangs time on the tables.|{season == "winter": Snow is coming down outside, and nobody is going anywhere.|The fire flares at the chorus, every time.}}
text [ff2612] = {一位老常客站在长凳上唱蝾螈酒馆的歌谣，唱那团永不熄灭的炉火。一共四十段。他记得大部分。|又是那首歌谣。今晚它有四十一段了；新的一段讲一个掉进地窖的学生。|歌谣里如今有一段唱城堡，唱到那里时常客们都看着你。} {老板娘假装讨厌这首歌。|满屋子人拍着桌子打拍子。|{season == "winter": 窗外正下着雪，谁也不打算走。|每到副歌，炉火就蹿高一下。}}
# en: A crowded low-beamed tavern, an old regular standing on a bench by the fire with a tankard raised, singing, while the room bangs time on the tables.
scene [c870d8] = 拥挤的矮梁酒馆里，一位老常客站在炉边长凳上举着酒杯高歌，满屋子人拍着桌子打拍子。
# en: Stand up and add a verse
opt.left.label [db3294] = 站起来添一段
# en: {You make up a verse about the landlady's slate and the room roars. She pours you a cider on the house, scowling.|You rhyme "Newt" with "absolute" and the whole tavern sings it back. You'll hear it for weeks.|Your verse about the castle gets a chorus of its own. The old regular claps you on the back and says you'll go in the ballad.}
opt.left.say.1 [c9e6ad] = {你即兴编了一段唱老板娘的记账石板，满屋哄堂。她板着脸请你喝了一杯免费的苹果酒。|你用“蝾螈”押上了“圆满”，整个酒馆跟着唱回来。你会听上好几个星期。|你那段唱城堡的歌词有了自己的副歌。老常客拍着你的背说，你会被写进歌谣里。}
# en: {You stand up, open your mouth and forget every word in the language. The old regular finishes your verse for you, kindly, and badly.|Your rhyme for "Newt" is "Newt". The room is silent, then merciless.|You sing your verse to the wrong tune. Half the room follows you and half the right one, and it ends in a brawl of harmonies.}
opt.left.say.2 [99e082] = {你站起来，张开嘴，把这门语言里的每个词都忘了。老常客好心地替你唱完了那段，唱得很糟。|你给“蝾螈”押的韵是“蝾螈”。满屋先是一片寂静，然后毫不留情。|你用错了调子。半屋子人跟着你，半屋子跟着正调，最后成了一场和声斗殴。}
# en: Buy the singer a drink
opt.right.label [7d8d29] = 请歌手喝一杯
# en: {You buy the old regular a cider, and he tells you the verses that aren't allowed in the ballad any more. They're the best ones.|You buy him a drink between verses. He toasts you in verse forty-two, which is new.|You buy the singer his usual. He tells you which verses are true. It's fewer than you'd hoped.}
opt.right.say.1 [d7359f] = {你请老常客喝了杯苹果酒，他告诉你那些如今不许唱的段落。那几段最好听。|你在两段之间请他喝了一杯。他在第四十二段里向你敬酒，这段是新的。|你请歌手喝了他常喝的那种。他告诉你哪些段落是真事。比你希望的少。}

@event mabels_fourth_cake
# en: The Fourth Cake
title [8c74a8] = 第四种蛋糕
# en: {Mabel's has three kinds of cake. Today, on a plate beside them, there is a fourth. "Experimental," says Mabel. "Free, if you're brave, petal."|Another fourth cake. Mabel has started a little card for each one: name, date, survivors.|The fourth cake. Mabel slides it across before you've asked, in case today is the day you're brave.} {This one is blue.|This one is suspiciously plain.|{season == "winter": It smells of cloves and something like snow.|It's still warm and very slightly humming.}}
text [e95740] = {梅布尔茶馆有三种蛋糕。今天，它们旁边的盘子里有第四种。“试验品，”梅布尔说，“胆子大就免费，小宝贝。”|又一个第四种蛋糕。梅布尔开始给每一个做小卡片了：名字、日期、幸存者。|第四种蛋糕。你还没开口梅布尔就推了过来，以防今天正是你胆大的日子。} {这块是蓝色的。|这块朴素得可疑。|{season == "winter": 它闻起来有丁香和某种像雪的味道。|它还温着，还在轻轻哼鸣。}}
# en: A tea-shop counter with three familiar cakes under glass domes and a fourth, mysterious one on a plate beside them, a woman in an apron watching expectantly.
scene [57baf8] = 茶馆柜台上，三种熟悉的蛋糕罩在玻璃罩下，旁边一只盘子里放着神秘的第四种，一位系围裙的女士满怀期待地看着。
# en: Be brave and try it
opt.left.label [42f3bf] = 大胆尝一口
# en: {It tastes exactly like the first warm day of spring. Mabel writes "a triumph" on her card.|It tastes of your grandmother's kitchen, or a kitchen you wish had been hers. Mabel watches your face and nods, satisfied.|It tastes like good news. Mabel says this one's going on the menu, and names it after the face you made.}
opt.left.say.1 [4a85e8] = {它尝起来恰似春天第一个暖和的日子。梅布尔在卡片上写下“大获成功”。|它尝起来像你祖母的厨房，或者你希望是她的那个厨房。梅布尔看着你的表情，满意地点点头。|它尝起来像好消息。梅布尔说这款要上菜单，还要用你当时的表情给它命名。}
# en: {It tastes of a memory of being scolded. Mabel takes it back, apologising, and writes "no" on her card.|It tastes of nothing at all, so completely that it's alarming. Mabel looks crestfallen.|It tastes of rainy afternoons in a waiting room. You can't explain it and never want to again.}
opt.left.say.2 [874caa] = {它尝起来像被训斥的记忆。梅布尔连声道歉地收回去，在卡片上写了个“不”。|它什么味道都没有，没有得如此彻底，令人心惊。梅布尔很是沮丧。|它尝起来像下雨天坐在候诊室的下午。你解释不了，也再也不想尝了。}
# en: Stick with your usual
opt.right.label [bbd386] = 还是要老样子
# en: {You order your usual. Mabel sighs, and cuts it a little larger than usual anyway, as if to make up for your cowardice.|You stick with the lemon slice. Mabel feeds the experiment to a delighted first-year, who turns briefly blue.|"Your usual, petal?" Mabel already has it on a plate. The fourth cake waits for someone braver.}
opt.right.say.1 [901b0f] = {你点了老样子。梅布尔叹口气，照样切得比平常大一点，像在弥补你的胆小。|你还是要柠檬切片。梅布尔把试验品喂给一个兴高采烈的一年级生，那孩子短暂地变蓝了。|“老样子，小宝贝？”梅布尔已经装好盘了。第四种蛋糕留给更勇敢的人。}

@event mabels_regulars_table
# en: The Regulars' Table
title [3625ea] = 常客的圆桌
# en: {The big round table at Mabel's belongs to the village regulars, four old friends, a box of dominoes and fifty years of arguments. They wave you over. "Settle something for us."|The regulars wave you over again. Today's dispute is about the academy in their day, when, they say, the stairs moved twice as often.|The regulars have saved you a chair. They've started calling you "the referee".} {The dominoes are clicking.|One of them was a student at the castle sixty years ago, and won't let anyone forget it.|{season == "winter": The window behind them is fogged from the teapots.|Mabel brings them more tea without being asked.}}
text [81592e] = {梅布尔茶馆那张大圆桌属于镇上的常客：四位老朋友、一盒多米诺骨牌和五十年的争吵。他们招手叫你过去。“给我们评评理。”|常客们又招手叫你了。今天争的是他们那时候的学院，他们说，那时楼梯挪动得比现在勤一倍。|常客们给你留了把椅子。他们开始叫你“裁判”了。} {多米诺骨牌哗啦作响。|其中一位六十年前在城堡念过书，谁都别想让他忘了提。|{season == "winter": 他们身后的窗户被茶壶熏得起了雾。|梅布尔不等吩咐就给他们添茶。}}
# en: A big round table in a tea shop crowded with elderly villagers playing dominoes and arguing, one of them waving a student over.
scene [f38683] = 茶馆里一张大圆桌旁挤满了玩多米诺骨牌、争吵不休的老镇民，其中一位正招手叫一个学生过去。
# en: Join the domino game
opt.left.label [c5541c] = 加入骨牌局
# en: {You keep count of every tile played and win a whole crown off a retired miller who swears he let you. He didn't.|You win, and the old student declares that the academy has gone soft and been lucky. You'll take it.|You win, and the regulars demand a rematch next time. "The referee's been practising."}
opt.left.say.1 [a03087] = {你记下了打出的每一张骨牌，从一位退休磨坊主那儿赢了整整一个克朗，他发誓是让着你。他没有。|你赢了，那位老校友宣布学院如今变软了，你是运气好。你照单全收。|你赢了，常客们要求下次再战。“裁判练过了。”}
# en: {The retired miller cleans you out with a smile like a closing door.|You lose to a woman of ninety who plays with her eyes shut.|You lose, and the regulars toast your generosity. Mabel brings you a consolation biscuit.}
opt.left.say.2 [f660fb] = {退休磨坊主带着关门似的笑容把你赢了个精光。|你输给了一位闭着眼打牌的九十岁老太太。|你输了，常客们举杯感谢你的慷慨。梅布尔给你端来一块安慰饼干。}
# en: Listen to their stories
opt.right.label [3d7422] = 听他们讲故事
# en: {You hear about the year a professor turned the refectory into a pond by accident, and the year someone taught the stairs to waltz. Half of it might be true.|The old student describes the castle as it was: the same stairs, different shoes. It's strange to hear your life told back sixty years early.|You referee three arguments and hear four stories. Your tea goes cold. It's worth it.}
opt.right.say.1 [b5857d] = {你听说有一年一位教授不小心把膳堂变成了池塘，还有一年有人教会了楼梯跳华尔兹。大概一半是真的。|老校友描述城堡当年的样子：同样的楼梯，不同的鞋。听你的生活提前六十年被讲回来，感觉很奇妙。|你裁决了三场争论，听了四个故事。你的茶凉了。值得。}

@event grimsbys_by_the_nose
# en: Chosen by the Nose
title [9eeed6] = 用鼻子挑书
# en: {Mr Grimsby holds three books under your nose, one after another, eyes closed. "Don't look. Smell. The right book smells right."|Mr Grimsby greets you with a book already held out at nose height. "Vanilla and rain," he says. "Trust me."|Mr Grimsby hands you a book by its smell before you've closed the door. He hasn't asked what you came in for. He never does.} {One smells of pipe smoke and the sea.|One smells of cut grass and arguments.|{season == "winter": One smells of woodsmoke, and the shop is freezing.|One smells, faintly, of you.}}
text [8407f2] = {格林斯比先生闭着眼，把三本书依次凑到你鼻子底下。“别看。闻。对的书闻起来就对。”|格林斯比先生迎接你时，手里已经举着一本书，高度正好在鼻子前。“香草和雨，”他说，“相信我。”|你还没关上门，格林斯比先生就凭气味递给你一本书。他没问你来买什么。他从来不问。} {有一本闻起来是烟斗和海。|有一本闻起来是青草和争吵。|{season == "winter": 有一本闻起来是柴烟，而店里冷得要命。|有一本隐约闻起来像你。}}
# en: An elderly bookseller holding closed books under a student's nose one at a time, eyes shut in rapture, shelves leaning overhead.
scene [60b8fc] = 一位年迈的书商把合着的书一本本凑到学生鼻子下，闭着眼一脸陶醉，头顶的书架东倒西歪。
# en: Buy the one that smells right
opt.left.label [0dd259] = 买闻起来对的那本
# en: {You buy the one that smells of the sea. It's a book of storms, beautifully written and of no use whatsoever. You love it.|Vanilla and rain is a slim book of poems about lighthouses. Mr Grimsby wraps it like a gift and takes your coin as an afterthought.|You buy the one that smells like you. It's a novel about someone your age on the night before they leave home. You read it on the barge, slowly.}
opt.left.say.1 [d90229] = {你买了闻起来像海的那本。是一本写风暴的书，文笔优美，毫无用处。你爱它。|“香草和雨”是一本写灯塔的薄诗集。格林斯比先生像包礼物一样包好，顺手才想起收你的钱。|你买了闻起来像你的那本。是一部小说，写一个和你同龄的人离家前的那个夜晚。你在驳船上慢慢读完了。}
# en: Insist on the one you came for
opt.right.label [3058bb] = 坚持要你来买的那本
# en: {You describe the book four times. On the fifth, Mr Grimsby lights up and produces it from under a cat-sized stack. He seems a little disappointed in you.|You stand firm. Mr Grimsby sighs, sniffs the air and goes straight to the right shelf. He could do this all along.|You've learned to describe a book by its smell. Mr Grimsby finds yours in a minute, beaming at your progress.}
opt.right.say.1 [b5eee2] = {你把那本书描述了四遍。第五遍时，格林斯比先生眼睛一亮，从一摞猫那么高的书底下把它抽了出来。他似乎对你有点失望。|你寸步不让。格林斯比先生叹口气，嗅了嗅空气，径直走到对的书架前。他一直都会。|你学会了用气味描述一本书。格林斯比先生一分钟就找到了，为你的进步笑逐颜开。}
# en: {You ask for a textbook and leave, somehow, with nothing at all, after an hour's lecture on the smell of old maps.|Mr Grimsby goes into the shelves for your book and is gone so long you leave a note.|Mr Grimsby brings you a cookbook, with great confidence, and is so hurt when you decline it that you stay an hour to make up for it.}
opt.right.say.2 [bbfa6b] = {你来买一本教科书，结果听了一小时关于旧地图气味的讲座，不知怎的空手而归。|格林斯比先生钻进书架去找你的书，一去不返，你只好留了张字条。|格林斯比先生信心满满地给你拿来一本菜谱，你婉拒时他伤心极了，你只好多待一小时来弥补。}

@event grimsbys_upper_floor
# en: The Upper Floor
title [7f6c6e] = 楼上
# en: {A ladder at the back of Grimsby's climbs through a hatch to an upper floor nobody mentions. "The remainders," says Mr Grimsby vaguely. "Mind the third rung. And the fourth."|The ladder to the upper floor. Someone has tied a ribbon round the third rung, as a warning or a memorial.|The upper floor. You know its geography now: poetry slumps against history, and history has given up.} {Dust swirls in the light from the hatch.|Somewhere up there, something slides and thumps.|{season == "summer": It's stifling under the roof.|Rain drums on the roof right above your head.}}
text [b75cd6] = {格林斯比书店后头有架梯子，穿过一个活板门通到一层没人提起的楼上。“清仓书，”格林斯比先生含糊地说，“小心第三级。还有第四级。”|通往楼上的梯子。有人在第三级上系了根丝带，不知是警告还是纪念。|楼上。你如今熟悉它的地形了：诗歌瘫靠在历史上，历史已经放弃了。} {活板门透进的光里尘埃飞旋。|楼上某处，有什么东西滑下来，咚的一声。|{season == "summer": 屋顶底下闷得透不过气。|雨点就在你头顶上方的屋顶上咚咚作响。}}
# en: A rickety ladder rising through a hatch in a bookshop ceiling into a dim upper room where shelves lean at alarming angles.
scene [cecdc6] = 书店天花板的活板门里伸出一架摇摇晃晃的梯子，通向一间昏暗的阁楼，书架倾斜得令人心惊。
# en: Climb up and rummage
opt.left.label [60f324] = 爬上去翻找
# en: {You find a first edition priced at a coin, with a pressed love letter inside. Mr Grimsby buys the book back at twice the price without noticing; the letter you keep.|You dig out a box of old exam papers from the castle, decades old. Mr Grimsby gives them to you for nothing and then pays you to take the box away.|You find a book of spells nobody casts any more, wedged under a shelf to stop it falling. Mr Grimsby gives you a crown for straightening the shelf.}
opt.left.say.1 [737c5d] = {你找到一本标价一枚硬币的初版书，里面夹着一封压平的情书。格林斯比先生没留意，用两倍价钱把书买了回去；情书你留下了。|你翻出一箱几十年前的城堡旧考卷。格林斯比先生白送给你，又付钱请你把箱子搬走。|你找到一本如今没人施的咒语书，被塞在书架底下防它倒。格林斯比先生给了你一个克朗，谢你把书架扶正。}
# en: {The third rung breaks, as advertised. You land in a heap of atlases and see stars, and some constellations.|A shelf leans on you, gently, and then less gently. You climb down under a small avalanche of poetry.|The fourth rung, this time. Mr Grimsby looks up from his counter, says "Ah," and goes back to his reading.}
opt.left.say.2 [ff81d3] = {第三级断了，正如预告。你摔进一堆地图集里，眼冒金星，还看见了几个星座。|一排书架轻轻靠在你身上，然后不那么轻了。你在一场小小的诗歌雪崩中爬了下来。|这回是第四级。格林斯比先生从柜台后抬头，说了声“啊”，又接着看书。}
# en: Browse the window display
opt.right.label [56d386] = 浏览橱窗陈列
# en: {The window display is arranged by colour, not subject. You find three books you didn't know you wanted, and want none of them enough to buy.|You browse the window, where the books have faded through thirty summers. It's a lovely, useless hour.|You browse the window and watch the village go by through the gaps between the spines.}
opt.right.say.1 [16dc6b] = {橱窗按颜色而非主题陈列。你发现了三本你不知道自己想要的书，却没有一本想要到要买。|你浏览着被三十个夏天晒褪了色的橱窗。美好又无用的一小时。|你浏览橱窗，透过书脊间的缝隙看小镇人来人往。}

@event pell_apothecary_back_door
# en: Foragers at the Back Door
title [7c4537] = 后门的采集人
# en: {At Pell's back door a forager in muddy boots is waiting to sell the morning's haul from the Whisperwood. She catches your eye. "Cheaper than the counter, love. No questions."|The forager at the back door again, basket heavier, prices lower. She remembers you.|The back-door forager nods at you like an old business partner. Today's basket has something in it that's still moving.} {The basket smells of moss and rain.|There's moonpetal in it, wrapped in a dock leaf.|{season == "winter": Her fingers are blue with cold.|Old Pell can be heard counting aloud inside.}}
text [329520] = {佩尔药铺的后门口，一个穿着泥靴的采集人等着卖掉早上从低语森林采来的货。她朝你使了个眼色。“比柜台便宜，亲爱的。不问来路。”|后门的采集人又来了，篮子更沉，价钱更低。她记得你。|后门的采集人像对老生意伙伴一样朝你点头。今天的篮子里有样东西还在动。} {篮子里有青苔和雨水的气味。|里面有月瓣花，用酸模叶包着。|{season == "winter": 她的手指冻得发青。|里头传来老佩尔大声数数的声音。}}
# en: A muddy forager with a basket of wild roots and mushrooms lingering at the back door of an apothecary, beckoning to a student in academy robes.
scene [3ebb85] = 一个满身泥泞的采集人提着一篮野根和蘑菇，在药铺后门徘徊，朝一个穿学院长袍的学生招手。
# en: Buy straight from her basket
opt.left.label [d7ed6c] = 直接从篮子里买
# en: {You buy a bundle of roots for half the counter price and spend the evening sorting the useful from the merely muddy.|You buy the moonpetal, dock leaf and all. It's the real thing; you can tell by the way it doesn't wilt.|You buy the moving thing, which turns out to be a root that wriggles toward water. You learn a great deal keeping it alive.}
opt.left.say.1 [025ffc] = {你用柜台一半的价钱买了一捆根，晚上花了一整晚把有用的和纯粹沾泥的分开。|你买下了月瓣花，连酸模叶一起。是真货；从它不肯蔫就看得出来。|你买下了那个会动的东西，原来是一条会朝水扭动的根。为了让它活下去，你学到了很多。}
# en: Ask where she found it all
opt.right.label [a40297] = 问她都在哪儿采的
# en: {She tells you about a clearing west of the stream where the moss glows. You write it down and do not go there, yet.|She tells you which mushrooms lie about being safe. It's an education, and it's free.|She tells you, lowering her voice, about a stream that runs uphill on nights of the full moon. Then she laughs and says it's probably nothing.}
opt.right.say.1 [98f86d] = {她告诉你溪水西边有片空地，那里的青苔会发光。你记下来，暂时没去。|她告诉你哪些蘑菇会谎称自己无毒。这是一堂课，还是免费的。|她压低声音，说有条小溪在满月夜往山上流。然后笑着说大概没什么。}

@event pell_apothecary_humming_drawer
# en: The Drawer That Hums
title [4c27a9] = 会哼鸣的抽屉
# en: {One of Pell's thousand drawers is humming, low and steady, like a kettle thinking about it. Its label has worn away.|A humming drawer again. Somebody has taped a fresh label to it: ASK FIRST.|The humming drawer has a new label in Old Pell's precise hand: NOT TODAY. It's a different drawer from last time.} {Both daughters are busy with a queue.|Old Pell is counting aloud in the back, loudly.|{season == "winter": The shop is cold, and the drawer is the only warm thing in it.|The bell over the door has just rung, and nobody has come in.}}
text [d45c34] = {佩尔家一千个抽屉里有一个在哼鸣，低沉而平稳，像一把正在考虑要不要烧开的水壶。它的标签已经磨没了。|又是一个会哼鸣的抽屉。有人在上面贴了张新标签：“先问”。|会哼鸣的抽屉上有了老佩尔一丝不苟的笔迹写的新标签：“今天不行”。不是上回那个抽屉了。} {两个女儿都在忙着应付排队的人。|老佩尔在后头大声数着数。|{season == "winter": 店里很冷，只有这个抽屉是暖的。|门上的铃刚响过，却没有人进来。}}
# en: A wall of a thousand small labelled drawers in an apothecary, one of them faintly rattling and humming, a student's hand hovering near its brass knob.
scene [5a1383] = 药铺里一整面墙的小标签抽屉，其中一个微微晃动、哼鸣着，一个学生的手悬在它的黄铜把手旁。
# en: Open it, just a crack
opt.left.label [9ad18d] = 拉开一条缝
# en: {Inside is a nest of dried bee-balm, humming with old summer. The smell follows you all day, and you know it now by heart.|Inside, a single seed pod is vibrating like a plucked string. You close it gently and remember its name.|Inside is a bottle of something that sings when the cork is loose. You tighten the cork and the shop goes quiet with relief.}
opt.left.say.1 [074cb0] = {里面是一窝干蜂香草，带着旧夏天嗡嗡作响。那股香味跟了你一整天，如今你已烂熟于心。|里面，一颗种荚像被拨动的弦一样震颤。你轻轻关上，记住了它的名字。|里面是一瓶软木塞一松就唱歌的东西。你拧紧瓶塞，整间铺子如释重负地安静下来。}
# en: {It's sneezing powder, enchanted to share itself. You sneeze until the queue applauds.|A puff of sleep-dust comes out. You wake on the floor with a daughter fanning you and Old Pell counting your breaths, aloud.|It's itching-seed, and it's in your sleeves. A daughter hands you a jar of ointment and a look.}
opt.left.say.2 [639943] = {是会自我分享的喷嚏粉。你打喷嚏打到排队的人鼓掌。|一股睡粉喷了出来。你醒来时躺在地上，一个女儿在给你扇风，老佩尔在大声数你的呼吸。|是痒痒籽，钻进了你的袖子。一个女儿递给你一罐药膏，外加一个眼神。}
# en: Ask a daughter what it is
opt.right.label [91adb4] = 问女儿里面是什么
# en: {"Bee-balm from a summer that didn't end," says the elder daughter, not looking up. "Leave it." You look it up later. She's right, and it's fascinating.|The younger daughter tells you it's a seed pod that hums before rain, and has never been wrong. You check the sky. She's right.|The daughters argue over what's in it for ten minutes. You learn more from the argument than from either answer.}
opt.right.say.1 [505b5f] = {“一个没结束的夏天的蜂香草，”大女儿头也不抬，“别碰。”后来你查了查。她说得对，而且很有意思。|小女儿告诉你那是一颗下雨前会哼鸣的种荚，从没错过。你看了看天。她说得对。|两个女儿为里面是什么争了十分钟。你从争论里学到的比从任何一个答案里都多。}

@event home_cottage_neighbour_calls
# en: A Neighbour Calls
title [1292c6] = 邻居来访
# en: {A neighbour is at the kitchen door with a stopped clock, a hopeful face and the air of someone who has been saving it for you since harvest.|Another neighbour, another hopeful face. This one has a hen that's laying eggs the wrong colour.|The neighbours have a list now, you suspect. Today, a pie that won't rise and won't explain why.} {Your family pretends not to listen.|Someone at the table says, "Go on, then," with pride.|{season == "winter": There's snow on the neighbour's hat; they've walked a long way.|The neighbour has brought a basket of plums, as payment in advance.}}
text [86aba7] = {一位邻居站在厨房门口，拿着一座停了的钟，满脸期待，看样子从秋收起就留着等你回来。|又一位邻居，又一张期待的脸。这位的母鸡下的蛋颜色不对。|你怀疑邻居们如今有张清单了。今天：一个不肯发起来、也不肯解释为什么的馅饼。} {你的家人假装没在听。|桌边有人说：“去吧，露一手。”语气里透着骄傲。|{season == "winter": 邻居的帽子上落满了雪；他们走了很远的路。|邻居带来一篮李子，算是预付的报酬。}}
# en: A neighbour in a muddy coat standing at a cottage kitchen door holding a stopped clock, while the family pretends not to listen from the table.
scene [52625c] = 一位穿着沾泥外套的邻居站在小屋厨房门口，抱着一座停了的钟，家人在桌边假装没在听。
# en: Have a go at it
opt.left.label [f3be98] = 试试看
# en: {You coax the clock's spring awake with a whisper. It chimes, a bit sheepishly. The neighbour tells the whole lane.|You charm the hen's eggs back to brown, more or less. The neighbour insists on giving you a dozen. They're mostly brown.|You find the trouble with the pie: it was sulking. A warm word and it rises. The neighbour's face rises with it.}
opt.left.say.1 [acbe36] = {你低声一句，把钟的发条哄醒了。它有点不好意思地敲响了。邻居告诉了整条巷子。|你把母鸡的蛋施咒变回了棕色，大致上。邻居坚持送你一打。大部分是棕色的。|你找到了馅饼的毛病：它在闹脾气。一句暖心话，它就发了起来。邻居的脸也跟着亮了起来。}
# en: {The clock starts running backwards, cheerfully. The neighbour leaves delighted, which is somehow worse, and tells the whole lane.|The eggs come out tartan. The neighbour is polite about it, and tells everyone.|The pie rises, and keeps rising, and leaves by the chimney. The whole lane will talk about it for years.}
opt.left.say.2 [894b94] = {钟开始欢快地倒着走。邻居心满意足地走了，这不知怎的更糟，还告诉了整条巷子。|蛋变成了格子花纹。邻居客客气气的，然后告诉了所有人。|馅饼发了起来，一直发，最后从烟囱里出去了。整条巷子会念叨好些年。}
# en: Say you're on holiday
opt.right.label [ebe5f2] = 说自己在放假
# en: {You smile and say magic is for term time. The neighbour goes away disappointed, and you have the afternoon to yourself by the fire.|You send them to the tinker, who will charge them, but kindly. You put your feet up.|You say no, gently. Your family exchange a look. You spend the afternoon asleep in your old chair, guilty and rested.}
opt.right.say.1 [e2387c] = {你笑着说魔法是学期里的事。邻居失望地走了，你独自守着炉火过了一下午。|你把他们打发去找补锅匠，他会收钱，但心肠好。你把脚翘了起来。|你温和地拒绝了。家人交换了一个眼神。你在自己的旧椅子里睡了一下午，又内疚又歇足了。}

@event home_market_schoolmistress
# en: The Old Schoolmistress
title [364f2d] = 老女教师
# en: {In the market you're stopped by the old schoolmistress who taught half the town its letters. "Come and tell my little ones about the academy," she says. "They won't believe me."|The schoolmistress again, with her satchel of slates. "The offer stands. They still don't believe me."|The schoolmistress waves from across the square. The children at her heels are wearing paper wizard hats, badly folded.} {She looks smaller than she used to.|She smells of chalk, as she always did.|{season == "winter": Her breath steams; she's been out in the cold looking for you.|A market dog is following her for the biscuits in her pocket.}}
text [58b194] = {你在集市上被那位教会半个镇子识字的老女教师拦住了。“来给我的小家伙们讲讲学院吧，”她说，“他们不信我。”|又是那位女教师，背着一袋石板。“邀请还算数。他们还是不信我。”|女教师在广场那头冲你挥手。跟在她身后的孩子们戴着折得歪歪扭扭的纸巫师帽。} {她看上去比从前矮小了。|她身上有粉笔味，一如既往。|{season == "winter": 她呵着白气；她一直在寒风里找你。|一条集市上的狗跟着她，惦记着她口袋里的饼干。}}
# en: A small elderly woman with a satchel of slates stopping a student in academy robes in the middle of a busy market street.
scene [adcda5] = 熙攘的集市街上，一位背着一袋石板的矮小老妇人拦住一个穿学院长袍的学生。
# en: Visit the schoolroom
opt.left.label [ddfa76] = 去教室看看
# en: {You tell twenty children about the moving stairs and the floating candles. One asks if you've met a dragon. You lie a little. They swarm you like bees.|You show them a single small flame in your palm. Twenty faces light up. You're exhausted after an hour, the good way.|You answer questions until your voice gives out. One of them wants to go to the academy now, very badly. It's your fault, and you're glad.}
opt.left.say.1 [e2151d] = {你给二十个孩子讲会动的楼梯和漂浮的蜡烛。有个孩子问你见没见过龙。你撒了个小谎。他们像蜜蜂一样把你围住。|你在掌心托起一小簇火苗。二十张脸亮了起来。一小时后你累坏了，是好的那种累。|你回答问题直到嗓子哑了。有个孩子现在非常、非常想去学院。都怪你，而你很高兴。}
# en: Buy her tea and listen
opt.right.label [1f66da] = 请她喝茶听她说
# en: {You buy her a pot of tea and she tells you which of your old classmates married whom, and which ran off to sea. You'd forgotten you missed them.|She asks what you're studying and actually listens. Then she corrects your grammar, out of habit, and you let her.|You buy her tea and she tells you what you were like at seven. It's alarming how little you've changed.}
opt.right.say.1 [a24874] = {你请她喝了一壶茶，她告诉你哪个老同学娶了谁、嫁了谁，哪个跑去出了海。你都忘了自己想念他们。|她问你在学什么，而且真的在听。然后她出于习惯纠正了你的语法，你由她去了。|你请她喝茶，她告诉你七岁时的你是什么样子。你变化之小令人吃惊。}
